.TH ISATTY 3
.SH NAME
isatty \- find out whether a file descriptor is a terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
int
isatty(fildes)
int fildes;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B isatty
returns 1 if the open file descriptor
.I fildes
is a terminal, and 0 if it is not, as for a file or a pipe. It asks
the terminal driver for the terminal's modes with
.BR ioctl (2),
which succeeds only for a terminal.
.PP
A program uses it to behave one way for a person at a terminal and
another for a file:
.BR man (1)
sends its pages through
.B more
only when its output is a terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
ioctl(2), termio(7)
.SH HISTORY
The
.B isatty
function first appeared in Version 7 AT&T UNIX.
